#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-firstrun.docbook:1
#, no-c-format
msgid "Getting Started"
msgstr "Comezar"

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-firstrun.docbook:7
#, no-c-format
msgid "The First Run Dialog"
msgstr "O primeiro diálogo de execución"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-firstrun.docbook:16
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "When you start &digikam; for the very first time it will ask you where you store your photographs and the &digikam; database. You can choose any local, remote or removable folder. Just type in the path name of a folder or click on the <guilabel>folder</guilabel> icon <inlinemediaobject> <imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"&path;introductionfoldericon.png\" format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject> <textobject> <phrase>Folder Icon</phrase> </textobject> </inlinemediaobject> to select a folder from the dialog."
msgid "When you start &digikam; for the very first time, it will ask you where you store your photographs. You can choose any local, remote or removable folder. Just type in the path name of a folder or click on the <guilabel>Browse...</guilabel> icon to select a folder from the dialog."
msgstr "Ao iniciar o &digikam; pola primeira vez, este pregunta onde se desexa gardar as fotografías e a base de datos do &digikam;. Pódese escoller calquera cartafol local, remoto ou retirábel. Simplemente escriba o nome completo dun cartafol ou prema a icona dun <guilabel>cartafol</guilabel>  <inlinemediaobject> <imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"&path;introductionfoldericon.png\" format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject> <textobject> <phrase>Icona de cartafol</phrase> </textobject> </inlinemediaobject> para escoller un cartafol no diálogo."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-firstrun.docbook:20
#, no-c-format
msgid "Later on you can add as many locations as you like - &digikam; will add them to the album library. <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure digiKam</guimenuitem><guimenuitem>Collections</guimenuitem></menuchoice>"
msgstr "Con posterioridade é posíbel engadir tantos lugares como se desexe - &digikam; engádeos á biblioteca de álbums. <menuchoice><guimenu>Configuración</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configurar digiKam</guimenuitem><guimenuitem>Coleccións</guimenuitem></menuchoice>"

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-firstrun.docbook:27
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "Choosing database path for digikam"
msgid "Choosing database path for &digikam;"
msgstr "Escolla da ruta á base de datos do digikam"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-firstrun.docbook:31
#, no-c-format
msgid "Then you have to specify a local folder that resides on your computer, in which the database will be stored. This path will be the same for all image folders. For details about the database type selection have a look at <link linkend=\"intro-database-intro\">The &digikam; Database</link>. If you have a local installation and a collection of less than 30.000 photographs you may well keep the default setting (SQLite)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-firstrun.docbook:41
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "Next, you will have to choose the way you would like to open RAW files : either with automatic adjustments or with the digiKam RAW import tool to adjust corrections manually."
msgid "Next, you will have to choose the way you would like to open RAW files: either with automatic adjustments or with the digiKam RAW import tool to adjust corrections manually."
msgstr "A continuación, hai que escoller como se desexa abrir os ficheiros RAW: con axustes automáticos ou coa ferramenta de importación de RAW de digiKam para axustar as correccións manualmente."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-firstrun.docbook:45
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "If you don't know what is a RAW file or if your camera don't support RAW files, you should keep the default setting and skip this step."
msgid "If you don't know what a RAW file is, or if your camera doesn't support RAW files, you should keep the default setting and skip this step."
msgstr "Se non sabe o que é un ficheiro RAW ou se a súa cámara non admite ficheiros RAW, hai que manter a opción por omisión e saltar este paso."

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-firstrun.docbook:52
#, no-c-format
msgid "RAW import"
msgstr "Importación de RAW"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-firstrun.docbook:56
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "Metadata information storage may be important if you plan to work with another photo management program and you should <guilabel>Add information to files</guilabel>. But if you don't want to alter your pictures, keep the default setting: <guilabel>Do nothing</guilabel>."
msgid "Metadata information storage may be important if you plan to work with another photo management program and you should choose <guilabel>Add information to files</guilabel>. But if you don't want to alter your pictures, keep the default setting: <guilabel>Do nothing</guilabel>."
msgstr "O almacenamento da información dos metadatos pode ser importante se pretende traballar con outro programa de xestión de fotos e debería <guilabel>Engadir información aos ficheiros</guilabel>. Mais se non quere alterar as imaxes, manteña a opción por omisión: <guilabel>Non facer nada</guilabel>."

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-firstrun.docbook:63
#, no-c-format
msgid "Metadata information"
msgstr "Información dos metadatos"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-firstrun.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid "Then choose how digiKam will load images in preview mode and light table. Reduced version will load faster but at the cost of quality."
msgstr "A continuación, escolla como desexa que digiKam cargue as imaxes no modo de previsualización e na mesa de luces. As versións reducidas cárganse máis rápido a cambio da perda de calidade."

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-firstrun.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid "Preview image method"
msgstr "Método de previsualización de imaxes"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-firstrun.docbook:78
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "Now how digiKam will open images on a right click. Previews will load faster but you won't be able to make any corrections."
msgid "Now decide how digiKam will open images with a click of the &RMB;. Previews will load faster but you won't be able to make any corrections."
msgstr "Agora, como abre as imaxes cun clic do botón esquerdo do rato. As vistas previas cárganse máis rápido pero non é posíbel facer correccións."

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-firstrun.docbook:85
#, no-c-format
msgid "Open image method"
msgstr "Método para abrir as imaxes"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-firstrun.docbook:89
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "Tooltips are a fast and easy way to display important information on a photograph, they popup as the mouse move over a thumbnail. Select \"Use tooltips\" if you want to display them."
msgid "Tooltips are a fast and easy way to display important information about a photograph; they popup as the mouse hovers over a thumbnail. Select \"Use tooltips\" if you want to display them."
msgstr "As suxestións son unha maneira rápida e fácil de amosar información importante sobre unha fotografía; aparecen cando o rato pasa por riba dunha miniatura. Escolla «Usar suxestións» se quere velas."

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-firstrun.docbook:96 intro-firstrun.docbook:107
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tooltips"
msgstr "Axudiñas"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-firstrun.docbook:100
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click on <guibutton>Finish</guibutton>. DigiKam will now start to scan for photographs..."
msgstr "Prema <guibutton>Rematar</guibutton>. digiKam comeza a buscar fotografías…"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-firstrun.docbook:111
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "If you already have a collection of photographs on your hard disk, you can enter the top-level folder containing the photographs, this is called the Albums Library folder. &digikam; will treat each sub-folder of the folder you've entered as an Album. None of the photographs will be altered. During folders parsing you can see a progress dialog like this:"
msgid "Nothing really to select here. You can cancel or start the scan with <guilabel>Finish</guilabel>. None of the photographs will be altered. During folders parsing you can see a progress bar in the lower right corner like this:"
msgstr "Se xa dispón dunha colección de fotografías no disco duro, pode introducir o cartafol superior que as conteña; chámase Cartafol da biblioteca de álbums. O &digikam; trata cada sub-cartafol do cartafol introducido como un álbum. Non se altera ningunha das fotografías. Durante a análise dos cartafoles pódese ver un diálogo da evolución semellante a este:"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-firstrun.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid "&digikam; will recurse the library path to its full depth. You cannot exclude (prune) any sub-path unless you make that sub-path hidden. You have to do that from outside of &digikam; by putting a dot in front of the sub-path."
msgstr "&digikam; examina recursivamente a ruta da biblioteca. Non se pode excluír (podar) ningunha subruta a non ser agochándoa. Haino que facer desde fóra de &digikam; poñendo un punto diante da subruta."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-firstrun.docbook:127
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "As &digikam; uses your folders on your hard disk directly, other applications like file managers can remove any albums outside a &digikam; session. In this case &digikam; will tell you at the next session if all albums that have been removed from the &digikam; photographs root path shall be deleted from albums database. If you want to move folders around and do not want to do that in &digikam;, we suggest you do that while &digikam; is running, so the database will be kept in sync and you do not lose any metadata."
msgid "As &digikam; uses your folders on your hard disk directly, other applications like file managers can remove any albums outside a &digikam; session. In this case &digikam; will ask you at the next session whether all albums that have been removed from the &digikam; photographs root path shall be deleted from albums database. If you want to move folders around and don't want to do that in &digikam;, we suggest you do that while &digikam; is running, so the database will be kept in sync and you do not lose any metadata."
msgstr "Dado que o &digikam; usa os cartafoles existentes no disco duro directamente, outros aplicativos, como xestores de ficheiros, poden eliminar álbums cando non se estea nunha sesión do &digikam;. Neste caso, o &digikam; pregunta na súa seguinte sesión se se quere retirar da base de datos os álbums que se eliminasen. Se quere reorganizar os cartafoles e non o quere facer no &digikam;, suxerimos que se faga mentres o &digikam; estea en execución para que así a base de datos siga sincronizada e non se perdan metadatos."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-firstrun.docbook:131
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "When you use an existing folder of photographs, as the Album Library folder, you will notice that the Albums in the Album list do not have photographs as their icons. You can change that by dragging any photograph in the Album onto the folder icon in the left sidebar and use this as the Album icon. See the <link linkend=\"using-myalbumsview\">Album</link> section for details of how to change the Album icon."
msgid "When you use an existing folder of photographs as the Album Library folder, you will notice that the Albums in the Album list do not have photographs as their icons. You can change that by dragging any photograph in the Album onto the folder icon in the left sidebar and use this as the Album icon. See the <link linkend=\"using-mainwindow-albumsview\">Album</link> section for details of how to change the Album icon."
msgstr "Cando se use un cartafol de fotografías existente como cartafol da biblioteca de álbums, vese que os álbums da lista de álbums non teñen fotografías como icona. Pódese modificar isto arrastrando calquera fotografía do álbum para a icona do cartafol na barra de ferramentas da esquerda e usar isto como icona do álbum. Vexa a sección sobre <link linkend=\"using-myalbumsview\">álbums</link> para detalles sobre como cambiar a icona dos álbums."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-firstrun.docbook:135
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "If you have previously accessed your photograph collection with another application, that has created thumbnails in non-standard sub-folders, &digikam; will show these thumbnail folders as separate Albums. &digikam; follows the <ulink url=\"http://www.freedesktop.org/\">freedesktop.org</ulink> standards for thumbnail folders. There is no way of hiding non-standard thumbnail folders from the &quot;Albums&quot; list. If you want to keep them you could create an Album Collection that just contains all the thumbnail Folders and then view your Albums in By Collection order. See the <link linkend=\"using-myalbumsview\">Album</link> section for more about Album Collections."
msgid "&digikam; uses a dedicated database to store thumbnails with an optimized wavelets compression algorithm (PGF). There is no way of hiding non-standard thumbnail folders from the <quote>Albums</quote> list. If you want to keep them you could create an Album Category that just contains all the thumbnail Folders and then view your Albums in <menuchoice><guimenu>View</guimenu><guimenuitem>Sort Albums</guimenuitem><guimenuitem>By Category</guimenuitem></menuchoice> order. See the <link linkend=\"using-mainwindow-albumsview\">Album</link> section for more about Album Categories."
msgstr "Se previamente accedeu á colección de fotografías con outro aplicativo que crease miniaturas en sub-cartafoles non padrón, o &digikam; mostra estes cartafoles como álbums separados. O &digikam; segue o estándar da <ulink url=\"http://www.freedesktop.org/\">freedesktop.org</ulink> para os cartafoles de miniaturas. Non hai maneira de agochar os cartafoles de miniaturas que non sigan o estándar da lista de &quot;álbums&quot;. Se quere mantelos, podería crear unha colección de álbums que simplemente conteña todos os cartafoles de miniaturas e así ver os álbums ordenados por colección. Vexa a sección sobre <link linkend=\"using-myalbumsview\">álbums</link> para máis sobre as coleccións de álbums."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5
#: intro-firstrun.docbook:139
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "Once you have configured the Album Library Folder you can set up &digikam; to work with your digital camera. Then learn how to use <link linkend=\"using-myalbumsview\">Albums</link> and <link linkend=\"using-mytagsview\">Tags</link> to arrange your photograph Albums."
msgid "Once you have configured the Album Library Folder you can set up &digikam; to work with your digital camera and then learn how to use <link linkend=\"using-mainwindow-albumsview\">Albums</link> and <link linkend=\"using-mainwindow-tagsview\">Tags</link> to arrange your photograph Albums."
msgstr "Unha vez configurado o cartafol da biblioteca de álbums, pódese configurar o &digikam; para que funcione cunha cámara dixital. A seguir, aprenda como usar os <link linkend=\"using-myalbumsview\">álbums</link> e as <link linkend=\"using-mytagsview\">etiquetas</link> para organizar os álbums de fotografías."
